{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeightAttack","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeightAttack","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Basic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.linearIndependent_not_algebraicallyIndependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.linearIndependent_not_algebraicallyIndependent","kind":"theorem","line":303,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TowerHeightAttack.lean#L303-L319","doc":"**Linear independence does not imply algebraic independence.**\n\n`t`, `t²`, `t³` are linearly independent as functions, yet annihilated by\n`z − x·y`. So a full-rank jet Jacobian — which is exactly a linear-independence\ncertificate — cannot by itself support an algebraic-independence conclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.closed_above_window","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.closed_above_window","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TowerHeightAttack.lean#L252-L266","doc":"**Closure above a vanishing window.** Once `D` consecutive levels vanish,\nthe order-`D` recurrence closes the tower from there on: `Φ_n = 0` for every\n`n ≥ N`. This is the finite-height conclusion the contrapositive needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.recurrence_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.recurrence_step","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TowerHeightAttack.lean#L232-L250","doc":"**The recurrence step — where the effective height comes from.**\n\nA relation of `q`-degree `D` convolves grade `k` of the relation with grade\n`n − k` of the tower, so the grade-`n` equation is\n`Σ_{k ≤ D} c_k · Φ_{n−k} = 0` — an order-`D` linear recurrence. With\n`c₀ ≠ 0`, a vanishing window of the `D` preceding levels forces `Φ_n = 0`.\n\nHence `h(P) = deg_q P`: the height bound is read off the relation, with no\narithmetic input. Effectivity is free once the tower is graded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.gradewise_closure_propagates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.gradewise_closure_propagates","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TowerHeightAttack.lean#L224-L230","doc":"Closure transfers level-by-level under a gradewise relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.gradewise_determines_level","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.gradewise_determines_level","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TowerHeightAttack.lean#L214-L222","doc":"**A gradewise relation determines each level.**\n\nContrast with §1: when the relation holds at every grade rather than only on\nthe totals, level `n` of one tower is pinned to level `n` of the other. This is\nthe whole difference between the failed and the repaired inference. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.perpetual_excludes_baseline","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.perpetual_excludes_baseline","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TowerHeightAttack.lean#L195-L210","doc":"**No `CSEvaluationFaithful` over a perpetual tower can use a\n`baselineDecomposition`.**\n\n`baselineDecomposition` sets `Φ_n = 0` for `n ≥ 1` — a tower closed at height\n`0`. Faithfulness over a perpetual tower forces every `Φ_n ≠ 0`. The two are\ncontradictory, so the corpus's only concrete decompositions\n(`volumeTowerDecomp_4_1/5_2/B3`, all baseline) cannot instantiate step 3 of the\ncontrapositive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.geomDecomp_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.geomDecomp_relation","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TowerHeightAttack.lean#L175-L191","doc":"The same counterexample packaged as two genuine `VolumeTowerDecomposition`s\nover one brane tower — every level non-zero, totals satisfying `3·A − 2·B = 0`.\n\nStated with a *single* universe-carrying binder (`tower`) and both\ndecompositions derived from it, per §7d U4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.relation_does_not_force_closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.relation_does_not_force_closure","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TowerHeightAttack.lean#L146-L173","doc":"**The stated inference fails.**\n\nThere exist two tower decompositions — over *any* brane tower — with **every**\nlevel contribution non-zero, whose totals satisfy the non-trivial ℚ-linear\nrelation `3·A − 2·B = 0`.\n\nA relation among the totals is one real equation; it cannot reach the\nindividual levels. Since linear relations are polynomial relations, this\nrefutes the general step *\"a polynomial relation would force the holonomy\ncontributions to close up after finitely many levels\"* for the **ungraded**\n`VolumeTowerDecomposition` the corpus actually defines.\n\nScope-(a): a statement about this inference, not about the conjecture. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.geomDecomp_total","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.geomDecomp_total","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TowerHeightAttack.lean#L142-L144","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.geomDecomp_level","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.geomDecomp_level","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TowerHeightAttack.lean#L138-L140","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.geomDecomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TowerHeight.geomDecomp","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TowerHeightAttack.lean#L119-L136","doc":"Geometric tower with ratio `r`, every level non-zero, total `s·(1-r)⁻¹`.\nUsed to package the counterexample as a genuine `VolumeTowerDecomposition`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}